{# Shared deny contexts - the OpenLiteSpeed counterpart of the nginx
   templates' `location ... { deny all; }` blocks, kept in one file so the two
   backends cannot drift apart in what they protect.

   Everything here was verified against a live OpenLiteSpeed server, because
   the obvious translations do not work:

   - `RewriteRule ... [F]` does NOT deny on OLS. A POST to xmlrpc.php still
     answered 200 with the full XML-RPC method list. Only accessControl does.
   - A regex context whose pattern is not anchored at the end is treated as a
     directory: `^/\.(?!well-known)` made /.htaccess answer 301 to
     /.htaccess/ instead of 403. Anchoring with `.*$` fixes it.
   - The negative lookahead really is honoured, so the ACME challenge under
     /.well-known keeps working - checked, not assumed.

   These must be emitted BEFORE `context /` so the more specific match wins. #}
{% for blocked in exact_denied | default([]) %}
context {{ blocked }} {
    location              {{ root_path }}/{{ document_root }}{{ blocked }}
    accessControl {
        deny              ALL
    }
}

{% endfor %}
{% for pattern in regex_denied | default([]) %}
context exp:{{ pattern }} {
    accessControl {
        deny              ALL
    }
}

{% endfor %}
